{"document":{"type":"root","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Defined in: "},{"type":"link","href":"https://github.com/TanStack/pacer/blob/main/packages/pacer/src/async-debouncer.ts#L218","children":[{"type":"text","value":"async-debouncer.ts:218"}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"A class that creates an async debounced function."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Async vs Sync Versions:\nThe async version provides advanced features over the sync Debouncer:"}]},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Returns promises that can be awaited for debounced function results"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Built-in retry support via AsyncRetryer integration"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Abort support to cancel in-flight executions"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Cancel support to prevent pending executions from starting"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Comprehensive error handling with onError callbacks and throwOnError control"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Detailed execution tracking (success/error/settle counts)"}]}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The sync Debouncer is lighter weight and simpler when you don't need async features,\nreturn values, or execution control."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"What is Debouncing?\nDebouncing ensures that a function is only executed after a specified delay has passed since its last invocation.\nEach new invocation resets the delay timer. This is useful for handling frequent events like window resizing\nor input changes where you only want to execute the handler after the events have stopped occurring."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Unlike throttling which allows execution at regular intervals, debouncing prevents any execution until\nthe function stops being called for the specified delay period."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Error Handling:"}]},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"If an "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"onError"},{"type":"text","value":" handler is provided, it will be called with the error and debouncer instance"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"If "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"throwOnError"},{"type":"text","value":" is true (default when no onError handler is provided), the error will be thrown"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"If "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"throwOnError"},{"type":"text","value":" is false (default when onError handler is provided), the error will be swallowed"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Both onError and throwOnError can be used together - the handler will be called before any error is thrown"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The error state can be checked using the underlying store"}]}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"State Management:"}]},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The debouncer uses a reactive store for state management"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Use "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"initialState"},{"type":"text","value":" to provide initial state values when creating the async debouncer"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The state includes canLeadingExecute, error count, execution status, and success/settle counts"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"State can be accessed via the "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"store"},{"type":"text","value":" property and its "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"state"},{"type":"text","value":" getter"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The store is reactive and will notify subscribers of state changes"}]}]}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"example","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Example"}]},{"type":"code","value":"const asyncDebouncer = new AsyncDebouncer(async (value: string) => {\n  const results = await searchAPI(value);\n  return results; // Return value is preserved\n}, {\n  wait: 500,\n  onError: (error) => {\n    console.error('Search failed:', error);\n  }\n});\n\n// Called on each keystroke but only executes after 500ms of no typing\n// Returns the API response directly\nconst results = await asyncDebouncer.maybeExecute(inputElement.value);","lang":"ts"},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"type-parameters","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Type Parameters"}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"tfn","children":[{"type":"text","value":"TFn"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"TFn"},{"type":"text","value":" "},{"type":"emphasis","children":[{"type":"text","value":"extends"}]},{"type":"text","value":" "},{"type":"link","href":"../type-aliases/AnyAsyncFunction.md","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"AnyAsyncFunction"}]}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"constructors","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Constructors"}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"constructor","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Constructor"}]},{"type":"code","value":"new AsyncDebouncer<TFn>(